course: dictionary
lesson: 3217
title: Enquiry and inquiry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An enquiry is a question you ask to find something out. You can make an enquiry at a shop desk, by phone or by email when you want to know something. The word can also be spelled inquiry, and both spellings mean the same thing.
explain: Sometimes an enquiry is official. When something goes badly wrong, such as a serious accident, an official enquiry looks into it carefully to find the facts. Here enquiry means a careful search for the truth.
explain: Look at the words around it to find the meaning. In «a community of enquiry», the class is a group thinking a question through together, giving reasons and listening. Clues like question, find out, facts or reasons show which meaning fits.
fact: Enquiry means a question you ask to find something out.
fact: Enquiry can also be spelled inquiry, and the two spellings mean the same.
fact: An official enquiry is a careful look into something that went wrong, to find the facts.
fact: «Make an enquiry» means ask a question, often at a desk, by phone or by email.
fact: In science, enquiry means finding things out by asking questions and testing ideas.
exercise: «Please make an enquiry at the desk if you need help with your ticket.» What does enquiry mean here? | A loud noise in the hall | A large box for storing books | *A question you ask to find something out | A type of sports game
exercise: «After the crash, an enquiry looked into what went wrong.» What is the enquiry? | A new road sign | A race around the park | *An official look into the facts | A party to celebrate
exercise: Which is another spelling of enquiry? | Enquary | Enquiree | *Inquiry | Enquirey
test: In «a community of enquiry», what does the class do? | *Think a question through together, giving reasons | Sell tickets to visitors | Sleep quietly in rows | Shout answers at once
test: In science, what does enquiry mean? | A cooking recipe | Painting a picture | *Finding things out by asking questions and testing | Reading a menu
exam: Ella asks, «Can I make an enquiry about the train times?» What does she want to do? | Sing a song | Build a train | Break a window | *Ask a question to find out the times
